+The tests that type into the guest's serial console (the boot, loader and UI
+tests) have QEMU write the console's output to a file and read the
+keystrokes from a FIFO (`-chardev file,...,input-path=`). Don't put it on a
+socket: if the reader falls about 50 ms behind while the kernel prints,
+Haiku's x86 kernel turns its serial output off for the rest of the boot.
